# Used both for the worker's Cloudflare Pages link (build-worker-app.bat) and the local
# start-worker-app.bat fallback. Points the app at wherever the backend actually is.
#
# ── If the backend is deployed to Render (see backend/DEPLOYMENT.md) — the current plan ──
# Replace the line below with your Render service's URL, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://jsm-logistics-backend.onrender.com/api
#
# ── If instead the backend still runs on Ritvik's laptop via the ngrok tunnel ──
# (see WORKER-LAPTOP-SETUP.md) — use the ngrok domain instead:
#   1. Sign up for a free ngrok account: https://dashboard.ngrok.com/signup
#   2. Install the ngrok agent and run: ngrok config add-authtoken <your-authtoken>
#   3. In the ngrok dashboard, go to Universal Gateway -> Domains and copy your free
#      permanent "dev domain" (looks like abc-123-xyz.ngrok-free.dev) — it never changes.
#   4. VITE_API_BASE=https://YOUR-NGROK-DOMAIN.ngrok-free.dev/api
VITE_API_BASE=https://YOUR-BACKEND-URL/api
